' ==============================================================================
' @file 3-1-crisismap-use-cases.puml
' @brief Core use case diagram for the Crisis Map disaster management system.
'
' @details
' This artifact defines the primary actors and their interactions with the 
' Crisis Map platform. It captures the behavioral boundaries of the system, 
' detailing how citizens, disaster managers, and automated systems trigger 
' core business processes such as reporting disasters, managing resources, 
' and broadcasting alerts.
'
' Architectural Scope & Rationale:
' This model is explicitly scoped to the requirements and behavioral tier. 
' It focuses on user goals and system boundaries rather than implementation 
' specifics. Internal system logic, data storage, and UI workflows are 
' deliberately deferred to subsequent structural and behavioral models.
'
' System Requirements Addressed:
' This model establishes the functional baseline of the application by defining:
' - The primary and secondary actors interacting with the system.
' - The core functional requirements grouped by user goals.
' - The system boundaries and inclusion/extension relationships.
' - The privilege separation between standard users and system administrators.
'
' Author(s): Vlado Sruk
' Context: Software Engineering Course
'
' AI Usage Disclosure:
' Designed by Vlado Sruk. AI-assisted revision and documentation comments were
' reviewed by the author, who is responsible for the final content.
'
' Traceability Note:
' The use cases defined herein must strictly map to the implemented features 
' and functional testing suites. Any behavioral deviations introduced during 
' development must be retroactively updated in this model to maintain evidence 
' chain completeness from requirements to code.
'
' Diagram level: System Requirements
' Diagram type:  Use Case Diagram
' ==============================================================================

@startuml

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
    BorderColor #212529
    ' External systems are visually distinct from human actors.
    BackgroundColor<<external system>> #FFF3CD
    BorderColor<<external system>> #856404
}

skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor #E7F1FF
    BorderColor #0D6EFD
    ArrowColor #212529
}

' ==============================================================================
' Primary Actors
' ==============================================================================

actor User as "Application User"
actor Citizen as "Citizen\n(Registered)"
actor Visitor as "Visitor\n(Anonymous)"
actor Manager as "Disaster Manager"

' Citizen and Visitor are specialized user roles.
Citizen -|> User
Visitor -|> User

' Layout-only relationships.
Manager -[hidden]down-> Citizen
Citizen -[hidden]down-> Visitor

' ==============================================================================
' Secondary - Supporting Actors
' ==============================================================================

actor "OAuth / Identity Provider" as IdP <<external system>>
actor "Map Service" as Maps <<external system>>
actor "Notification Service" as Notifications <<external system>>

' ==============================================================================
' System Boundary
' ==============================================================================

rectangle "Crisis Map System" as CrisisMap {

    ' Access
    (Sign In / Authenticate) as UC_SignIn

    ' Reports and map
    (View Reports on Map) as UC_Map
    (Filter Incident Layers) as UC_Filter
    (Submit Disaster Report) as UC_Report
    (Validate Report Data) as UC_ValidateReport
    (Upload Photo Evidence) as UC_UploadPhoto

    ' Resource coordination
    (View Available Resources) as UC_Resources
    (Allocate Relief Resources) as UC_Allocate

    ' Alerts
    (Receive Proximity Alerts) as UC_Alert
}

' ==============================================================================
' Actor-to-Use-Case Associations
' ==============================================================================

' Common user capability
User -- UC_Map

' Anonymous visitor capability
Visitor -- UC_SignIn

' Registered citizen capabilities
Citizen -- UC_Report
Citizen -- UC_Alert

' Disaster manager capabilities
Manager -- UC_Resources
Manager -- UC_Allocate

' ==============================================================================
' UML Relationships
' ==============================================================================

' Optional behavior extending a complete base use case.
UC_Map <.. UC_Filter : <<extend>>\n[filter requested]

UC_Report <.. UC_UploadPhoto : <<extend>>\n[photo provided]

' Mandatory reused behavior performed during report submission.
UC_Report ..> UC_ValidateReport : <<include>>

' Authentication is intentionally NOT modeled as <<include>> for protected
' operations. A user may already be authenticated before starting them.
' Treat authentication as a precondition unless sign-in is always executed
' within the use case itself.

' ==============================================================================
' Secondary Actor Interactions
' ==============================================================================

UC_SignIn -right- IdP

' Map Service is deliberately shown in this educational diagram to expose an
' important external dependency. In a stricter goal-oriented model it may be
' shown only in architecture or deployment views.
UC_Map -right- Maps

' Keep this actor only if external notification delivery is part of the
' approved scope and implementation.
UC_Alert -right- Notifications

' Layout-only ordering for the external-system column.
IdP -[hidden]down-> Maps
Maps -[hidden]down-> Notifications

@enduml
